From b00f2a1901091b8a3222dc5576638684b36d95ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Diego Amicabile <diego.amicabile@soprasteria.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:04:57 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Borg: answer the endgame recall-depth prompt with 'y' as its
 comment says

borg_recall()'s branch for the Morgoth push (deepest level 99, fewer
than five uniques live) carried a comment saying to reset the recall
depth -- cleaning up the last uniques -- but pressed 'n' with a note
saying "Not Resetting recall depth." The stale half-comment about
keeping the potion stock came in with the changed key. Press 'y' and
note "Resetting recall depth." so later recalls land at the depth
where the remaining uniques are hunted.
---
 src/borg/borg-escape.c | 6 +++---
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/borg/borg-escape.c b/src/borg/borg-escape.c
index 79ef7add7..51efcc302 100644
--- a/src/borg/borg-escape.c
+++ b/src/borg/borg-escape.c
@@ -98,9 +98,9 @@ bool borg_recall(void)
                     else if (borg.trait[BI_MAXDEPTH] == 99
                         && borg_numb_live_unique < 5) {
                         /* Do reset Depth, cleaning up last uniques to hit */
-                        /* Morgoth.  Want to keep using up the stock of potions */
-                        borg_note("# Not Resetting recall depth.");
-                        borg_keypress('n');
+                        /* Morgoth. */
+                        borg_note("# Resetting recall depth.");
+                        borg_keypress('y');
                     }
                     else {
                         /* Do reset Depth */
-- 
